<% content_for :title, "Console library" %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>The console library</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every cart on this site runs against the same library, and it travels with
    your upload &mdash; there is nothing to install and nothing to require.
    This is console <%= @console_version.version %><%= ", the version a new upload is pinned to" if @console_version.default? %>.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="doc-note">
  <p>
    A cart is a directory with a contract: an entry file naming a class after
    the directory, and whatever art and data it needs beside it. Zip that
    directory, upload it, publish it. Everything below is what goes in the file.
  </p>
</div>

<section class="doc-section" id="get-it">
  <h2>Get the console</h2>
  <p>
    A cart runs on the console: a directory of Ruby, this library, and a small
    tool that boots it. Unpack the download into a checkout and the library is
    in place.
  </p>
  <p>
    <% if authenticated? %>
      <%= link_to "Download it with my publishing key", console_bundle_path, class: "button-link" %>
      <span class="muted">or <%= link_to "just the library", library_download_path %></span>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to "Download the library", library_download_path, class: "button-link" %>
      <span class="muted">
        &mdash; <%= link_to "sign in", new_session_path %> to download it with a
        key that lets you publish carts from the console.
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="doc-section" id="your-first-cart">
  <h2>Your first cart</h2>
  <% @guide.samples.each_with_index do |sample, index| %>
    <div class="doc-sample" id="<%= sample.id %>">
      <h3><%= sample.title %></h3>
      <p><%= sample.note %></p>
      <pre class="source"><%= raw FileHighlighter.new("sample.rb", sample.code).call %></pre>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>

<section class="doc-section" id="hooks">
  <h2>The hooks</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    Every hook is optional. A cart that defines none of them still boots &mdash;
    it just does nothing.
  </p>
  <table class="doc-table">
    <tbody>
      <% @guide.hooks.each do |hook| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code><%= hook[:name] %></code></td>
          <td class="doc-when"><%= hook[:when] %></td>
          <td><%= hook[:note] %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<section class="doc-section" id="publishing">
  <h2>Sending a cart here</h2>
  <p>
    No archive to build and no upload form. With the bundle unpacked and your key
    in it:
  </p>
  <pre class="source">./publish-site arcade</pre>

  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <% @guide.publishing[:steps].each do |step| %>
      <li><%= step %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>

  <p class="muted">
    The same upload, without the browser. Everything the form refuses it refuses
    &mdash; traversal, symlinks, expansion bombs, art a cart names but does not own
    &mdash; and it says so in the message.
  </p>

  <details class="doc-endpoint">
    <summary>The endpoint, if you are writing your own client</summary>
    <pre class="source"><%= raw FileHighlighter.new("client.rb", @guide.publishing[:endpoint].join("\n")).call %></pre>
  </details>
</section>

<section class="doc-section" id="reference">
  <h2>The API</h2>
  <p>
    <%= pluralize(@modules.size, "module") %>, described by the library's own
    comments. Nothing here is written by hand, so it cannot drift from the code
    it describes.
  </p>

  <ul class="doc-index">
    <% @modules.each do |mod| %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to mod.name, doc_path(mod.slug) %>
        <span class="doc-index-summary"><%= mod.summary %></span>
        <span class="muted"><%= pluralize(mod.sections.sum { |s| s.methods.size }, "method") %></span>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>